+
+| Claim | Result | Status | Run files |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| C1 | TUI renders `ask_user_question`; answer "Teal" reaches the scripted provider as the tool result; `[Extensions]` lists only `scripted-provider.ts` | proved | `runs/A-C1-tui.txt`, `runs/A2610-C1-tui.txt`, `runs/*-C1-scripted.jsonl` |
+| C2 | One `extension_ui_request` with method `select`; the response "1. Teal — The first option." becomes the tool result | proved | `runs/A-C2-rpc.jsonl`, `runs/A2610-C2-rpc.jsonl` |
+| C3 | Built-in loads under `noExtensions`; the extension registers `ask_user_question` in both sessions; `getAllTools()` lists it only when allowlisted; runtime enabling of a non-allowlisted built-in is refused | partly: holds when "tool registry" means extension registration, fails when it means `getAllTools()` | `runs/A-C3-C5-sdk.json`, `runs/A-C3-registry-detail.json`, A2610 equivalents |
+| C4 | A `DefaultResourceLoader` constructed in `spike/harness/` loads both hidden built-ins | proved | `runs/A-C3-C5-sdk.json`, `runs/A2610-C3-C5-sdk.json` |
+| C5 | `--list-models` lists `spike-fixture/echo`; `pi -p --model spike-fixture/echo` prints the echo; `modelRuntime.getModel` resolves; an SDK turn completes | proved | `runs/A-C5-cli.txt`, `runs/A-C3-C5-sdk.json`, A2610 equivalents |
+| C6 | Fenced `pi-fence run --profile general` of `dist/bundle/cli.js`, grants excluding `rpiv-mono` (`runs/C6-01-dry-run-after-edit.txt`): questionnaire renders, "Teal" reaches the provider, `[Extensions]` lists only the harness; the journal records only `auth.json` read denials and one DNS lookup, none under the worktree or `rpiv-mono` | proved, under Node 26.10.0 only | `runs/A2610-C6-fenced.txt` |
+| C7 | 12 added, 0 removed in upstream-owned files before the fixture; 13 with the fixture; ported directory byte-identical except `UPSTREAM.json`; modes equal; `npm run check` exit 0 | proved | `runs/A-C7-measure.txt`, `runs/A-07-check.log`, `runs/A2610-C7-measure.txt`, `runs/A2610-02-check.log` |
+
+Supporting conclusions, all proved by the named runs:
+
+- `scripts/check-pinned-deps.mjs` rejects `^2.11.0` in the ported `package.json`. One added exclusion line keeps byte parity and exempts `packages/builtins/` from the pin rule (`runs/A-04-check.log`, `runs/A-05-check.log`).
+- The shrinkwrap and install-lock generators need one added line each to accept a `packages/builtins/*` dependency of `packages/coding-agent`. The shrinkwrap then resolves the ported package to the upstream npm tarball, so a published `coding-agent` would install upstream's code, not the fork's (`runs/A-06-regenerate-locks.log`).
+- Each additional built-in costs one added line in `packages/coding-agent/package.json`, an upstream-owned file (`runs/A2610-C7-measure.txt`).
+- A process that imports `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` by bare specifier, with no fork entry, receives the built-ins (`runs/A2610-C4-direct-bare-only.json`).
