+# Candidate B findings (registry and distribution)
+
+All behavioral runs ran under Node 26.10.0, installed by Homebrew at 09:57:55 UTC during the run. Install, build, `npm run check` and C7 ran under 26.8.2 before that, and `npm run check` was repeated under 26.10.0.
+
+| Claim | Result | Status | Run files |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| C1 | Through `packages/distribution/bin/pi.mjs`: TUI renders `ask_user_question`; "Teal" reaches the scripted provider; `[Extensions]` lists only `scripted-provider.ts` | proved | `runs/B-C1-tui.txt`, `runs/B-C1-scripted.jsonl` |
+| C2 | One `select` request; the response becomes the tool result | proved | `runs/B-C2-rpc.jsonl` |
+| C3 | Same as candidate A through `packages/distribution/index.mjs`: extension registration in both sessions, `getAllTools()` filtered by the allowlist, runtime enabling refused | partly: same two readings as A | `runs/B-C3-C5-sdk.json`, `runs/B-C3-registry-detail.json` |
+| C4 | A loader constructed in `spike/harness/` loads both built-ins when the distribution entry was imported in the process | proved | `runs/B-C3-C5-sdk.json`, `runs/B-C4-direct-after-entry.json` |
+| C5 | `--list-models`, `-p` echo, `getModel` and an SDK turn all succeed through the distribution | proved | `runs/B-C5-cli.txt`, `runs/B-C3-C5-sdk.json` |
+| C6 | Fenced `pi-fence run --profile general` of `packages/distribution/bin/pi.mjs`, grants excluding `rpiv-mono` (`runs/C6-01-dry-run-after-edit.txt`): questionnaire renders, "Teal" reaches the provider, `[Extensions]` lists only the harness; the journal records only `auth.json` read denials and one DNS lookup, none under the worktree or `rpiv-mono` | proved | `runs/B-C6-fenced.txt`; failed first attempt `runs/B-C6-fenced-attempt1-trust-prompt.txt` |
+| C7 | 11 added, 0 removed in upstream-owned files; lock files unchanged; ported directory byte-identical except `UPSTREAM.json`; `npm run check` exit 0 | proved | `runs/B-C7-measure.txt`, `runs/B-02-check.log`, `runs/B-04-check-node2610.log` |
+
+Supporting conclusions, all proved by the named runs:
+
+- A process that imports `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` by bare specifier without importing the distribution entry receives no built-ins (`runs/B-C4-direct-bare-only.json`). The OpenIntent worker imports the SDK that way today, so candidate B meets the frozen restriction "an SDK consumer outside this repository must import a fork entry point".
+- Once the distribution entry is imported, a bare-specifier import resolves to the same `packages/coding-agent/dist/index.js` and shares the registry (`runs/B-C4-direct-after-entry.json`). An in-process extension such as `pi-subagents` therefore inherits the built-ins.
+- Additional built-ins cost zero lines in upstream-owned files; the fixture changed only the fork-owned `packages/distribution/package.json` (`runs/B-C7-measure.txt`).
+- `packages/coding-agent` never depends on a ported package, so the shrinkwrap and install-lock generators need no change (`runs/B-C7-measure.txt`, no generated-file rows).
+- B's `pi` bin runs the unbundled `dist/index.js`, not upstream's esbuild bundle `dist/bundle/cli.js`. Startup cost against the bundle was not measured.
+- `setupCli` needed one export line in `packages/coding-agent/src/index.ts`; copying its five statements into the distribution would drift from upstream.
+
+C6 procedure and side findings, shared by both candidates:
+
+- The operator approved removing the `rpiv-mono` entry from `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` for the C6 window. The coordinator backed the file up (SHA-256 `088a665e…`), removed one line and one comma, ran both C6 harnesses, verified the file still held the edited bytes (`8c31d900…`), and restored the backup byte-identically. The window ran from about 10:06 to 10:10 UTC.
+- Before the edit, the fence derived read grants for seven fork checkouts from `settings.json` packages, `rpiv-mono` among them (`runs/C6-00-dry-run-general.txt`). After the edit, `rpiv-mono` appears nowhere in the effective policy (`runs/C6-01-dry-run-after-edit.txt`).
+- The worktree carries a `.pi/` directory, so pi opens the project-trust dialog. Choosing "Trust" inside the fence crashes pi with an uncaught `EPERM` on `~/.pi/agent/trust.json`, which the fence does not grant for writing (`runs/B-C6-fenced-attempt1-trust-prompt.txt`). The harness answers "Do not trust (this session only)". The crash belongs to pi and pi-fence, not to either candidate.
+- pi-fence drops `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` from the child environment, so a fenced session always uses `~/.pi/agent` and its `settings.json`.
+- The pty driver runs outside the fence; `pi-fence run` wraps only the candidate's `pi`. This session is unfenced, so no sandbox nests. The operator approved this departure from the opin-spike rule that no harness starts a sandbox.
+- No subagent ran a harness. The coordinator read every claim from the raw run files named above.
